.SH UPGRADING
When upgrading from a previous BFD installation (including v1.5\-2),
.B install.sh
automatically backs up the existing installation to
.I /usr/local/bfd.bk.DDMMYYYY\-HHMMSS
(symlinked as
.IR /usr/local/bfd.bk.last )
and runs
.B importconf
to merge configuration and preserve state.
.PP
.B importconf
migrates: user configuration (conf.bfd values), legacy variable name
translations (TRIG \(-> PRESSURE_TRIP, BAN_DURATION \(-> BAN_TTL, etc.),
per\-rule overrides (thresholds.conf \(-> pressure.conf), firewall backend
detection, ban state (bans.active, bans.history, events.dat), log tracking
state (tlog byte\-offsets, journal cursors), custom alert templates, and
ignore lists.
.PP
Post\-upgrade verification:
.RS 4
.nf
bfd \-c          # health check and diagnostics
bfd \-\-status    # show current ban/event summary
.fi
.RE
.PP
To roll back, flush any new bans and restore the backup:
.RS 4
.nf
bfd \-\-flush\-all
rm \-rf /usr/local/bfd
cp \-a /usr/local/bfd.bk.last /usr/local/bfd
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
In watch mode
.RB ( "bfd \-w" ):
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration (conf.bfd, internals.conf, pressure.conf)
without restarting.
.TP
.B SIGTERM\fR, \fBSIGINT
Clean shutdown: release lock, exit gracefully.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error (invalid config, unknown option).
.TP
.B 2
Lock error (another instance running).
.TP
.B 3
Prerequisite error (missing tlog, rules directory, etc.).
